{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ce8bf2b1f8eef40","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-Readiness Assessment for Llama Stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's defining unknown: no systematic GA-readiness assessment of Llama Stack has been done, and the full inventory of gaps that Tech Preview status currently excuses is not known. This investigation inventories the gaps between current TP quality and the GA bar across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling, and produces the definitive GA scope that all downstream Llama Stack graduation work is planned against.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Define the GA-bar evaluation dimensions per the strategy: API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling.\n34\t- Audit the current Tech Preview state against each dimension, using the component's upstream and midstream source repositories, the platform distribution, and the TP feedback scattered across support tickets.\n35\t- Consolidate TP feedback from support tickets and map each item to a gap area.\n36\t- Produce a gap inventory that states, per gap: current state, GA bar, severity, and remediation sizing.\n37\t- Identify which gaps change the scope or approach of the API stability work, the quality remediation work, and the production support posture work.\n38\t- Output the definitive GA scope document, accepted by the owning team and product stakeholders as the basis for the graduation work.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- The gap inventory covers all four dimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with current state, GA bar, and gap recorded per item.\n43\t- TP feedback from support tickets is consolidated and mapped to inventory items.\n44\t- Each inventory item is classified by whether it affects the scope or approach of the stability, remediation, or support-posture work, so downstream scope can be finalized from the inventory alone.\n45\t- The resulting GA scope document is reviewed and accepted by the owning team and the product stakeholder as the definitive GA scope.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-1 (P0): directly delivers the GA-readiness assessment that inventories the gaps between current TP quality and the GA bar and produces the definitive GA scope.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-809f9020a2fe957d","agent_id":"abb62d5961a044b64","session_id":"d3f3ba1a-747f-4186-8293-bb365a6cbf67","uuid":"c4888895-e5ff-4db5-83ca-9c138ac1ba87","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:50:30.364Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ce8bf2b1f8eef40","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
