{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2f2f3be4168817e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'Missing DAG edge E003 -> E004: E003 scope/AC hands off characterized\n10\t    scale limits in a form the supported configuration matrix can consume, and E004\n11\t    scope/AC incorporates the scale limits characterized by the GA quality remediation\n12\t    work, yet E004 dependencies list only E001 and the summary DAG shows E003 and\n13\t    E004 as parallel branches — a data/artifact dependency between two implementation\n14\t    epics is not captured in the DAG (not a build-pipeline output, so the AC-gate\n15\t    carve-out does not apply)'\n16\t- severity: minor\n17\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n18\t  description: TrustyAI guardrails integration documentation is claimed by both E005\n19\t    (authoring usage/configuration/support-boundaries docs) and E007 (scope item Coverage\n20\t    of the supported TrustyAI guardrails integration); the summary says integration\n21\t    docs are intentionally not split into the docs epic, so sharpen the division so\n22\t    the content is authored once (E005 authors, E007 reviews/links)\n23\terror: null\n24\t---\n25\t## Review Summary\n26\t\n27\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n28\tRecommendation: revise\n29\t\n30\tcontract validator: OK (no violations). Triage consistency: `triage: null` (full\n31\tdecomposition), so the 7-epic output is expected and not penalized. Diagram\n32\tedges and epic frontmatter `dependencies` match exactly; no circular\n33\tdependencies; critical path length 3 fits the M-standard heuristic (3-4). The\n34\tfailure is a single structural defect: a data/artifact dependency between two\n35\timplementation epics (E003 → E004) that epic content makes explicit but the\n36\tDAG does not capture.\n37\t\n38\t## Criterion Details\n39\t\n40\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n41\tAll six HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 → E001 (assessment) + E003 (remediation of the\n42\tinventoried gaps), HLR-2 → E002, HLR-3 → E004, HLR-4 → E005, HLR-5 → E006,\n43\tHLR-6 → E007. Traceability matrix present in the summary and per-epic HLR\n44\tTraceability sections are consistent with it. Priority inheritance: E001 blocks\n45\tall P0 implementation work and is P0. E007's P0 is correct per the\n46\tdocs-authoring exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0), and\n47\tthe E005/E006 (P1) → E007 (P0) edges are Rule 11 edges that do not trigger\n48\tpriority inheritance — the summary records this analysis, so it is not an\n49\tunanalyzed inversion. No epic carries HLRs at mixed priority levels, so no\n50\tpriority collapse or bundling analysis is required; the one bundling judgment\n51\t(E005 keeping its integration documentation, per HLR-4's \"supported, documented\n52\tintegration\" wording) is recorded in the traceability matrix row with rationale.\n53\t\n54\t### 2. DAG Coherence (0/2)\n55\tDiagram/frontmatter consistency: every edge in the mermaid diagram has a\n56\tmatching `dependencies` entry in the target epic and vice versa; arrows run\n57\tdependency → dependent per convention; no invalid references; no cycles.\n58\tImplementation-type parallelism rules (7/8/10) do not apply — no\n59\tkonflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist. Rule 11\n60\tdocs-last coverage is complete (all five Implementation epics block E007). The\n61\tE002 ↔ E005 coupling over the versioned API surface is correctly expressed as\n62\tan acceptance criterion on E005 rather than an edge (Rule 14 parallel: different\n63\tteam and repo; the surface already exists in TP form). However, there is a\n64\t**critical missing edge**: E003's scope and acceptance criteria explicitly hand\n65\toff \"characterized scale limits ... in a form the supported configuration matrix\n66\tcan consume,\" and E004's 