cope still claims coverage — the division\n93\tshould be sharpened so the content is authored once (E005 authors, E007\n94\treviews/links). Not score-reducing on its own.\n95\t\n96\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n97\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (the definitive GA scope) changes\n98\twhat E002/E003/E004 do — the strategy's open question says so explicitly. All\n99\tthree gated epics set both `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001` (present in their\n100\tdirect `dependencies` lists) and `gate_failure_impact` with both `action` and\n101\t`fallback_approach` populated. E005/E006/E007 have no Investigation\n102\tdependencies and correctly leave `gated_by` null. All Implementation epics\n103\tproduce concrete artifacts. No misclassifications.\n104\t\n105\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n106\tType-appropriate signal fields used throughout: E001 carries\n107\t`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric); E002-E007 carry `ai_signals`\n108\t(9-signal rubric); no cross-assignment. Signal values are consistent with the\n109\trationales and the strategy content: E002/E003/E004 score `open_questions: -1`\n110\tmatching their gating on the assessment; E005/E006 score `open_questions: 1`\n111\tmatching their fixed-deliverable framing; E001's `human_judgment_required: -1`\n112\tmatches the stakeholder acceptance of the GA scope.\n113\t`architecture_claims: 1` across the implementation epics is correctly\n114\tcalibrated against `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`\n115\t(llama-stack.md, trustyai.md, dashboard.md) — the strategy's TP-status and\n116\tAPI-surface premises are corroborated and cited in the rationales, not asserted\n117\twithout a source. Computed aggregates (`ai_implementability`,\n118\t`ai_implementability_score`) are pipeline-computed and not checked.\n119\t\n120\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n121\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs:\n122\tE006 (default-enablement change) carries th