for entitled clusters.\n48\t- Technical review of all new and changed content against the implemented GA behavior.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Documentation meets GA documentation standards for the component.\n53\t- Migration notes cover the TP releases from which the upgrade path is tested.\n54\t- Support-posture documentation (SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix) is included and consistent with the published posture.\n55\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented GA behavior (API surface and upgrade path, support posture, guardrails integration, Dashboard enablement).\n56\t- Content is produced and published through the Red Hat docs content process.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-6 (P2): documentation uplifted to GA standards, including migration notes from TP. Epic priority is P0 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Critical), not by inheritance from the HLR's P2 label.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b8e084ffbbadeac","agent_id":"aaa91a67b57736f0a","session_id":"d3f3ba1a-747f-4186-8293-bb365a6cbf67","uuid":"90460aba-408b-4caa-bc47-07ab07422a42","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:54:45.879Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac6750c4a47da11a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
