lable without any opt-in action.\n45\t- On a non-entitled cluster, Llama Stack management surfaces remain hidden.\n46\t- The enablement can be disabled through Dashboard configuration without code rollback.\n47\t- Existing opt-in users see no regression in their management flows when the default flips.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-5 (P1): the Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a956c3fa5fc996c3","agent_id":"ae91568166fe76520","session_id":"d3f3ba1a-747f-4186-8293-bb365a6cbf67","uuid":"22c73403-0d59-478e-bd09-53d69d2fc521","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:57:04.535Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92e569d97501a37b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
